      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1440,
      "desc": "At some point, wearing all black became a visual label for urban and rural teenagers. Seen as undisciplined and reclusive, they still long to be seen and to belong.\nDingxing Vocational High School introduced the “Zhengcun Martial Lion” dance. Traditional culture became part of cherished youth memories and gained new vitality. As teenagers helped one another and traded places, their urge to express themselves blossomed; pure friendship challenged prejudice, creating mutual fulfillment.\nDingxing is a fortunate example. Many young people remain clouded by labels, still seeking a place to belong."
    },
