    {
      "id": "xiaomi-486d003ef9470715",
      "name": "Intertidal Zone",
      "userName": "Zeno of Citium",
      "sourceIds": [
        "xiaomi-2026-international-6ae041d7ba786a0001d90f65-ed0ac344c1b7d7306441f9df"
      ],
      "picUrl": "https://img.youpin.mi-img.com/ferriswheel/f16a80f1_f2c6_4868_8ae6_cd0fab76d075.jpeg?w=1440&h=1920",
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 1920,
      "desc": "Born in the inland, my dry and isolated childhood instilled in me an inexplicable longing for the sea—it was like a distant shore I had never reached but was always striving toward. This fascination drove me to set out time and again, from the Balkans to the Ryukyu Islands, from the Vestfjord to the Gold Coast… I try to gaze upon “existence” through my lens. In these unassuming images, life, death, and rebirth are no longer sharply distinguished; they ebb and flow like the tides, leaving behind damp traces—simply to prove that everything once happened."
    },
